  "mathematical_conclusions": [
    "The monic-selector-first universal resultant proof handles quadratic-to-linear/constant specialization, odd selector degrees and zero divisors through an integral polynomial identity.",
    "The production binary Lucas/Dickson updates preserve the intended T_n, T_(n+1), (AC)^n state, and S3 coefficient expansion matches the stated polynomial.",
    "The x=t leading-coefficient degree drop remains present and the finite linear/doubling branch is retained.",
    "Split-selector gcd support, root-count consistency, coordinate reconstruction and signed rational replay are consistent with the stated finite-target contract.",
    "The optional order check is accurately restricted to an annihilator condition, not a general certificate of membership in a specified cyclic subgroup.",
    "The schoolbook norm-stage O(d^2 log d) bound and separate root/lifting costs are appropriately distinguished from fast-polynomial possibilities and the O(d) signed-point scan."
  ],
